## Audit finding and change

- The reverse scan found 24 public helper types/functions under
  `rocketmq_classic_common::serde_fastjson`. Pinned Java 5.5.1 exposes public
  JSON operations through `FastJsonSerializer` and `RemotingSerializable`, but
  not equivalent public per-field coercion helpers; the helpers are DTO
  implementation plumbing.
- Made common's helper module private and retained only the `MessageQueue`
  conversion subset there. Protocol now owns the route/body/heartbeat adapters
  in a crate-private module. Rustdoc compile-fail examples guard both external
  import paths. Existing DTO parser behavior and Java fixture outcomes remain
  unchanged.
- The first visibility pass left unused common-side helpers and produced
  dead-code warnings. Reduced that module to its actual MessageQueue dependency
  closure; the final strict Clippy run is warning-free.
- Updated ADR-0014/0015, the Phase 6 audit, and release checklist. Plan files
  remain unchanged.

